// "[subject] draws N" ([CR#121.1]): the declarative-subject draw — that
// player draws N cards, one at a time ([CR#121.2] — a per-card sequence,
// not a simultaneous batch like mill). `Draws` is `Draw`'s twin: a
// `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit `By(who, Draw)`. The engine runs the N
// contained draws sequentially, each binding the library top late and
// empty-checking before its move, so an empty library loses the game
// ([CR#121.4,104.3c]).
//
// Not a keyword action ([CR#701] does not list drawing — it is [CR#121])
// and not a `Composite`: drawing is irreducible ([CR#121.5]), so there is
// no body. See `Draw.ron` for why the `KeywordAction` macro kind stays (it
// is the English verb registry, not a CR claim).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) is `By`'s agent — a real slot, not a coordinate scraped
// off a body selection. The template renders the subject context-aware
// ("Target player draws two cards.", "Each player draws a card."); the
// count spells its noun via the `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Draws(It, 1) (the announced player target / Each-bound player,
// Jace Beleren) / Draws(Target(0), 2).
(
    name: "Draws",
    template: "${0} draws ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    // Four frames: a guarded frame pre-binding Param(0) to `You` (the
    // dominant filler) and an unguarded frame spelling the subject out,
    // each doubled for count = 1 — `Count`'s `Numeral` hole only ever
    // matches a quantity determiner ("N cards"), never the indefinite
    // "a card", so count = 1 needs its own zero-hole literal in both forms.
    frames: [
        (text: "draw <Param(1)> cards", when: [(0, "You")], position: Main),
        "<Param(0)> draws <Param(1)> cards",
        (text: "draw a card", when: [(0, "You"), (1, "1")], position: Main),
        (text: "<Param(0)> draws a card", when: [(1, "1")]),
    ],
    body: Batch(Param(1), By(Param(0), DrawCard)),
)
